DEFINITIONS
  - WASHED: a loss sale with a replacement bought within 30 days either side (trade dates), IRAs included: disallowed (§1091), no still-held test; the loss moves into the replacement's basis (lost in an IRA).
  - BLOCKED: a loss sale in the last 30 days, some still held: a buy before the printed date disallows the loss on as many shares as you buy.
  - LOCKED: an IRA bought in the last 30 days: a taxable loss sale is a wash sale for that many shares, permanently (Rev. Rul. 2008-5).
  - EXITABLE: bought in a taxable account in the last 30 days: a FULL exit at a loss is fine, a partial loss sale is a wash sale.
  - COOLING: sold out at a loss recently: wait 31 days from the sale (trade date) before buying back.
  - RISK: sellable at a loss NOW, but an IRA still holds: an IRA buy (a DRIP too) within 30 days after disallows the loss permanently.
  - CLEAR: no recent buys; safe to sell at a loss (no buy-back for 30 days).
  - A long call bought in a loss's window is noted, not enforced; after a loss on covering a short only a new short sale replaces it (§1091(e)); futures and their options are §1256, outside §1091.

Scope: these verdicts cover this project's accounts only. A purchase by your spouse or by a corporation you control within 30 days before or after a loss sale also makes it a wash sale (§1091; IRS Pub. 550) — those accounts are not in the project, so check them yourself.
